  "problems": "Zara publishes no general women's body-measurement size chart: there is no size-guide help page (help-center/SizeGuide is 'PAGE NOT FOUND'), and product pages offer only a per-product 'Measurements' panel of FLAT GARMENT measurements plus an interactive 'Size recommender'. The two charts here are single-product garment examples, not a brand-wide chart; values are flat (half-circumference) and must not be compared directly with body measurements. Jeans panel also lists total length and rises (machine-translated as 'Front towing eye' / 'Backfire'), no inseam. Spain store labels the jeans EU 32-46; the Ireland store shows the same product as 4-18 (UK). Dress chart also has chest, total length, sleeve length, arm width (bust stored from 'Chest'). Inches toggle exists."
